---
import HearthPage from '../layouts/HearthPage.astro';
---
<HearthPage title="Council" description="The Council — who guides Hearth & Code." current="">
<header >
      <p >Council</p>
      <div class="hp-hero"><h1>The Council</h1></div>
      <p >In Hearth &amp; Code's vocabulary, the Council holds the values and guards the fire. Not a board or committee — the people who've accepted responsibility for what this is and what it's supposed to become.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="council-grid">
      <article >
        <div class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">SR</div>
        <div class="council-info">
          <span class="council-role">Hearth-Keeper</span>
          <h2>Scott Rallya</h2>
          <p>RPI Computer Science &amp; Psychology, 2007. Built software across fintech, healthcare, telephony, and media — stepped back in 2020 and started designing the thing that would have helped him get back. Now building Hearth &amp; Code from the ground up.</p>
          <div class="council-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/cosmatrexis" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
            <a href="/library/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Field Journal</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>The Council grows as Hearth &amp; Code grows. There are no open applications right now. If you've been following this and you have something to give — skills, time, perspective — the fire is open. Reach out at <a href="mailto:hello@hearthandcode.dev">hello@hearthandcode.dev</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div  style="justify-content: flex-start; margin-top: 56px;">
      <a  href="/about.html">About &rarr;</a>
      <a  href="/mission.html">Mission &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</HearthPage>
